{
  "feature": "Guided quickstart skill: env checks, sandbox provisioning, first canary run",
  "workflow_type": "simple",
  "workflow_rationale": "Single-service change: extend the /quickstart skill (markdown + one small shell script + one test). No cross-service dependencies, no data migration.",
  "phases": [
    {
      "id": "phase-1-env-check",
      "name": "Environment prerequisite checker script",
      "type": "implementation",
      "description": "Create a standalone, exit-coded prerequisite checker the skill can invoke, producing actionable errors for each missing prerequisite.",
      "depends_on": [],
      "parallel_safe": true,
      "subtasks": [
        {
          "id": "subtask-1-1",
          "title": "Create scripts/check_env.sh",
          "description": "Create `scripts/check_env.sh` modeled on the step/ok/warn/die helpers in `scripts/setup_sandbox.sh`. Checks, in order: (1) Python >= 3.11 (`python3 -c 'import sys; sys.exit(sys.version_info < (3,11))'`) with the install command in the error; (2) Docker CLI present and daemon reachable (`docker info`) with 'start Docker Desktop / install docker' guidance; (3) OS/arch support — Linux x86_64/aarch64 for gVisor, with explicit macOS/Windows message pointing at a Linux VM or `--dangerously-no-sandbox` (same wording as setup_sandbox.sh); (4) gVisor runsc installed (`runsc --version`, `/usr/local/bin/runsc`) — warn-only, pointing at `scripts/setup_sandbox.sh`; (5) `CLAUDE_CODE_SUBAGENT_MODEL` / model env hint — warn-only. Exit 0 when all hard checks pass (warnings allowed), exit 1 on any hard failure. Support `--json` flag emitting a small JSON summary for programmatic use by the skill. Bash, `set -euo pipefail`, SPDX header like other scripts.",
          "service": "repo",
          "files_to_modify": [],
          "files_to_create": ["scripts/check_env.sh"],
          "patterns_from": ["scripts/setup_sandbox.sh"],
          "verification": {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "bash -n scripts/check_env.sh && bash scripts/check_env.sh --json; echo exit=$?",
            "expected": "Valid JSON with per-check status; exit=0 or exit=1 matching environment"
          },
          "status": "pending"
        },
        {
          "id": "subtask-1-2",
          "title": "Add tests for check_env.sh",
          "description": "Create `tests/test_check_env.py` (pytest, subprocess-based) covering: script passes `bash -n`; `--json` output parses and contains keys python, docker, gvisor, os; hard-failure exit code is 1 when a check fails (simulate by overriding PATH or stubbing `docker` with a failing shim in tmpdir); warning-only checks do not cause exit 1. Follow the style of existing tests (plain pytest, tmp_path fixture).",
          "service": "repo",
          "files_to_modify": [],
          "files_to_create": ["tests/test_check_env.py"],
          "patterns_from": ["tests/test_sandbox.py", "tests/test_checkpoint.py"],
          "verification": {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "python3 -m pytest tests/test_check_env.py -q",
            "expected": "All tests pass"
          },
          "status": "pending"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "phase-2-skill",
      "name": "Extend /quickstart with guided pipeline path",
      "type": "implementation",
      "description": "Rewrite the Intro-mode options in .claude/skills/quickstart/SKILL.md to add a Step-2 guided path: env validation, sandbox provisioning, and a first canary pipeline run with expected outputs.",
      "depends_on": ["phase-1-env-check"],
      "parallel_safe": false,
      "subtasks": [
        {
          "id": "subtask-2-1",
          "title": "Add env-check and sandbox steps to SKILL.md",
          "description": "Modify `.claude/skills/quickstart/SKILL.md`: (1) add `Bash(bash scripts/check_env.sh:*)` and `Bash(bash scripts/setup_sandbox.sh:*)` to `allowed-tools` (skill still never executes target code itself — the pipeline command is given to the operator to run, or run via bin/vp-sandboxed only with explicit user confirmation); (2) extend the Intro-mode AskUserQuestion to four options, adding 'Set up and run the pipeline on the canary (~15 min)' which triggers a new 'Guided pipeline first run' section; (3) new section 'Guided pipeline first run' with steps: Step A — run `bash scripts/check_env.sh --json`, interpret each check, on hard failure print the actionable fix from the script and stop; Step B — if runsc missing, walk the operator through `bash scripts/setup_sandbox.sh` (confirm before running; it uses sudo and modifies /etc/docker/daemon.json), then re-run the check; Step C — confirm model env (`--model` flag or `VULN_PIPELINE_MODEL`), then have the operator run (with their approval) `bin/vp-sandboxed vuln-pipeline run targets/canary --runs 3 --parallel --stream --max-turns 100` explaining each flag in one line; Step D — describe expected outputs with exact paths: `results/canary/<ts>/found_bugs.jsonl`, `results/canary/<ts>/run_*/result.json`, `results/canary/<ts>/reports/bug_NN/report.json`, and that the first report typically lands within minutes; Step E — recap + pointer to README Step 2 and `docs/pipeline.md`. Keep the existing Help mode and Day-1 guided section unchanged except for cross-links.",
          "service": "repo",
          "files_to_modify": [".claude/skills/quickstart/SKILL.md"],
          "files_to_create": [],
          "patterns_from": [".claude/skills/threat-model/SKILL.md", ".claude/skills/quickstart/SKILL.md"],
          "verification": {
            "type": "manual",
            "instructions": "Review SKILL.md: frontmatter YAML parses (allowed-tools updated), new section references only real paths (scripts/check_env.sh, scripts/setup_sandbox.sh, bin/vp-sandboxed, targets/canary), pipeline command flags match harness/cli.py, no instruction has the skill execute target code unsandboxed."
          },
          "status": "pending"
        },
        {
          "id": "subtask-2-2",
          "title": "Add quickstart skill README",
          "description": "Create `.claude/skills/quickstart/README.md` documenting the three quickstart paths (30-sec intro, Day-1 static skills, pipeline readiness path), the prerequisite table (Python >=3.11, Docker, Linux for gVisor), the expected-output paths for a canary run, and the 15-minute budget breakdown. Follow the style of `.claude/skills/customize/README.md`.",
          "service": "repo",
          "files_to_modify": [],
          "files_to_create": [".claude/skills/quickstart/README.md"],
          "patterns_from": [".claude/skills/customize/README.md", ".claude/skills/triage/README.md"],
          "verification": {
            "type": "manual",
            "instructions": "README paths and commands cross-checked against SKILL.md and repo layout"
          },
          "status": "pending"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "phase-3-validation",
      "name": "Cross-check and full test suite",
      "type": "integration",
      "description": "Verify docs consistency and that nothing regressed.",
      "depends_on": ["phase-2-skill"],
      "parallel_safe": false,
      "subtasks": [
        {
          "id": "subtask-3-1",
          "title": "Run full test suite and consistency check",
          "description": "Run `pytest tests/` (docker-dependent patch tests may fail pre-existing on docker-less hosts — note them as pre-existing per .claude/skills/verify/SKILL.md). Grep SKILL.md/README.md for every file path and command referenced and confirm each exists in the repo (`scripts/check_env.sh`, `scripts/setup_sandbox.sh`, `bin/vp-sandboxed`, `targets/canary`, `docs/pipeline.md`). Confirm every CLI flag used appears in `harness/cli.py` argparse.",
          "service": "repo",
          "files_to_modify": [],
          "files_to_create": [],
          "patterns_from": [],
          "verification": {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "python3 -m pytest tests/ -q --ignore=tests/test_patch_grade_e2e.py; grep -oE '(scripts|bin|targets|docs)/[A-Za-z0-9_./-]+' .claude/skills/quickstart/SKILL.md .claude/skills/quickstart/README.md | sort -u | while read p; do [ -e \"$p\" ] || echo \"MISSING: $p\"; done",
            "expected": "All non-docker tests pass; no MISSING lines"
          },
          "status": "pending"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "verification_strategy": {
    "risk_level": "low",
    "skip_validation": false,
    "test_creation_phase": "post_implementation",
    "test_types_required": ["unit"],
    "security_scanning_required": false,
    "staging_deployment_required": false,
    "acceptance_criteria": [
      "scripts/check_env.sh validates Python >=3.11, Docker, OS/arch, gVisor with actionable errors and exits nonzero on hard failure",
      "check_env.sh has unit tests that pass",
      "/quickstart SKILL.md offers a guided path through env check, sandbox setup, and a canary pipeline run",
      "All paths and CLI flags referenced in skill docs exist in the repo",
      "Existing test suite unaffected (new tests only, no harness changes)",
      "Skill never executes target code itself; pipeline commands run via bin/vp-sandboxed or by the operator"
    ],
    "verification_steps": [
      {
        "name": "Unit Tests",
        "command": "python3 -m pytest tests/test_check_env.py -q",
        "expected_outcome": "All tests pass",
